212
00:16:14,068 --> 00:16:19,231
What it changes: it deletes a ref and its
reflog. What it can destroy: your only

213
00:16:19,271 --> 00:16:24,499
name for commits that are on no other
branch. How to preview: the tree comparison

214
00:16:24,539 --> 00:16:29,832
you saw. How to recover: git branch with
the name and the ID, and the ID is in the

215
00:16:29,872 --> 00:16:35,296
output, c0b29a8. When it's appropriate:
here, after you've shown that the content is

216
00:16:35,336 --> 00:16:35,816
on main.

217
00:16:36,156 --> 00:16:40,717
And the picture after the deletion: the
branch name is gone, and no branch reaches

218
00:16:40,757 --> 00:16:42,119
the two commits any more.

