234
00:18:03,896 --> 00:18:05,544
Five mistakes to watch for.

235
00:18:05,884 --> 00:18:11,829
A script reports exactly 30 items. Root
cause: lists return 30 items per page and

236
00:18:11,869 --> 00:18:14,416
the script did not pass --paginate.

237
00:18:14,756 --> 00:18:20,438
A script created something by accident. Root
cause: a field flag switched the method

238
00:18:20,478 --> 00:18:23,231
from GET to POST; -X GET keeps it a read.

239
00:18:23,571 --> 00:18:28,517
gh acts on the wrong one of fork and
upstream. Root cause: with two remotes there

240
00:18:28,557 --> 00:18:33,010
are two candidates, and no default was
recorded with gh repo set-default.

241
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:39,491
Reading a 404 as "the repository does not
exist". Root cause: for a private resource

242
00:18:39,531 --> 00:18:43,759
and a token without access the
API answers 404 on purpose.

243
00:18:44,099 --> 00:18:48,127
Building tooling on a personal
token and on human-readable output.

244
00:18:48,167 --> 00:18:52,934
Root cause: the token acts as one person
everywhere and stops when that person

245
00:18:52,974 --> 00:18:57,742
leaves, and the text output is not a
stable interface; use --json, the version

246
00:18:57,782 --> 00:18:59,283
header, and a GitHub App.

247
00:19:01,123 --> 00:19:06,421
Now, out of the lab. The textbook's case.
A nightly job lists the pull requests of

248
00:19:06,461 --> 00:19:10,979
sixty repositories with unauthenticated
curl. It worked from a laptop.

249
00:19:11,019 --> 00:19:16,057
It fails on the shared CI runner, where
the sixty requests per hour of that IP

250
00:19:16,097 --> 00:19:21,461
address are spent before the job starts.
Unauthenticated limits were lowered on the

251
00:19:21,501 --> 00:19:24,847
eighth of May 2025, anonymous
HTTPS clones included.

252
00:19:25,187 --> 00:19:30,278
The tempting repair is a retry loop. The
textbook's verdict: the fix is an identity

253
00:19:30,318 --> 00:19:35,472
for the job, not a retry loop. For an
evaluation dashboard on an AI and ML team that

254
00:19:35,512 --> 00:19:40,666
reads pull request data every night, the
identity is a GitHub App installed on those

255
00:19:40,706 --> 00:19:44,252
sixty repositories with read
permission for pull requests.

256
00:19:44,292 --> 00:19:49,384
The job then has its own rate limit, and
it survives the departure of whoever wrote

257
00:19:49,424 --> 00:19:49,569
it.

